From 7a20e2b965e506131d6bdff1c18352de59d9b390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:01:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Add the Estimated Service Parameters Inbound element

The Estimated Service Parameters Inbound element (IEEE Std 802.11-2024,
9.4.2.172) lets a STA estimate the throughput it would get from an AP
before associating (11.44); Wi-Fi Optimized Connectivity 3.15 requires
it, with the AC_BE parameters, in the Beacon and Probe Response frames
of an OCE AP. hostapd did not have it.

Add esp=1 to include the element. It carries the AC_BE parameters:
A-MPDU with a 64 MPDU block ack window and a 4 ms PPDU duration target
when HT is enabled, and, as the estimated air time fraction, the
channel time not used by other BSSs (channel busy time minus the
radio's own transmit time, from the survey data that the BSS Load
element uses) shared equally between a new STA and the associated STAs,
the model Wi-Fi Optimized Connectivity 3.15 describes. The element
therefore needs bss_load_update_period.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
 hostapd/config_file.c       |  2 ++
 hostapd/hostapd.conf        | 11 +++++++++
 src/ap/ap_config.h          |  1 +
